<objective>
Implement two features identified in the audit:

**1. Notification Routing** — lets GRC teams get alerted in Slack/email/webhook when compliance events occur (finding created, control failed, evidence expired). Closes gap versus Probo which has full notification routing.

**Notification channel schema:**
```json
{"id": "chan-{uuid}", "tenantId": "...", "type": "slack", "name": "Security Slack", "config": {"url": "https://hooks.slack.com/..."}}
```

**Routing rule schema:**
```json
{"id": "rule-{uuid}", "tenantId": "...", "event_type": "control_failed", "severity_filter": ["high","critical"], "channel_ids": ["chan-abc"]}
```

**2. Domain/Subdomain Scanner** — lightweight external attack surface scanner. Closes gap versus Probo's domain monitoring feature.

Domain scan returns:
```json
{
  "domain": "example.com",
  "subdomains": ["www.example.com", "api.example.com"],
  "open_ports": {"80": true, "443": true, "8080": false},
  "tls": {"expiry": "2026-12-01", "issuer": "Let's Encrypt", "san": ["example.com", "*.example.com"]},
  "dns": {"A": ["1.2.3.4"], "MX": ["mail.example.com"], "TXT": ["v=spf1..."], "NS": ["ns1.example.com"]}
}
```

Use Python's built-in `socket`, `ssl`, `dns.resolver` (dnspython package) for scan — no external services.

